      "problem": "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $2+6+18+⋯?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=2$ and $r=3.$ Therefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{2(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{2}(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & ={3}^{N}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
